            "notes": "## \ud83d\udcaa powers\n[Crepuscular Circle](item_c0b93ed2-b692-44d5-a38a-ce5a63e83cdb). the bread and butter of this build, and what makes Valk so game-winningly strong in Stadium.\n\n## \ud83d\udcb0 items\n[Chain Evoker](item_812cc89e-feb0-47d0-9e03-9d8e33a80aca) if you're ahead, [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) if you're behind. [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) almost always. after that, just fill up on blues and greens you can afford.\n\nalternatively, if you're not getting picked off and you're stinking rich, you can take [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) over [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) and fill up on blue WP items as shown :)\n\n## \u2753 how it works\nkeep flying between your teammates as normal, maximizing ult charge with [Threads of Fate](item_cb61612b-9d83-49a9-989d-013bf084fbcb). once you have Valk, press Q and whip out your blaster. [Crepuscular Circle](item_c0b93ed2-b692-44d5-a38a-ce5a63e83cdb) means you no longer have to hold your staff to heal and/or damage boost while ulting; it does BOTH automatically as long as you're close enough to your teammates. the range is pretty forgiving; just don't fly halfway across the map from them and you should be good.\n\n**important note:** while your staff normally stays attached to teammates through a wall for a couple seconds after you break line of sight, this is **not** the case for [Crepuscular Circle](item_c0b93ed2-b692-44d5-a38a-ce5a63e83cdb) buff. it will *not* apply to your teammates who are near you but behind a wall, around a corner, under a bridge, etc. position accordingly, and click those heads!",
