            "notes": "## \ud83d\udcb0 items\nat this point, you should be able to prioritize [Chain Evoker](item_812cc89e-feb0-47d0-9e03-9d8e33a80aca) if not already. this will help you farm ult charge much faster by blue beaming, leading to more Valks, more MVPs, more cash, rinse and repeat.\n\nhowever, there are situations in which you can't justify [Chain Evoker](item_812cc89e-feb0-47d0-9e03-9d8e33a80aca) despite your best efforts (you've been playing cover and using your pings, right?) in that case, here's what we can do:\n\n[Resurrection Rangefinder](item_99baffec-51b5-42e4-be61-e29f3de8219f) if someone is getting picked early consistently every fight\n\n[Caduceus Ex](item_9e7965ea-2abc-44a7-b042-950c6ad2fce7) for longer range maps where we need to stay back from our team, especially if they have an [Ashe](hero_37b42a2d-a82d-4a22-9df2-4c812c873b54) who's giving us trouble\n\n[Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) for even MORE healing by spamming our left shift\n\nin order, from top to bottom, is my preference of these alternatives. [Resurrection Rangefinder](item_99baffec-51b5-42e4-be61-e29f3de8219f) makes one of the strongest abilities in the game that much stronger, and [Caduceus Ex](item_9e7965ea-2abc-44a7-b042-950c6ad2fce7) is just nice QoL. [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) is *very* strong if you're good at using it, but i'm just honestly not. it requires you to spam your guardian angel to build and maintain stacks, which can leave you vulnerable at critical moments in teamfights.",
