            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-24T06:18:53.276562+00:00",
            "notes": "## \ud83d\udcaa powers\n[Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1) is my go-to. it gives your team the extra layer of survivability often needed to clutch out these last teamfights. however, there are viable alternatives:\n\n[Battle Medic](item_ccd0edff-4d57-4ac2-83a7-bab6ff0ffb2f) turns you into a tiny machine gun anytime you swap off your staff, and the buff uptime is infinite during the entire duration of Valk/mini-Valk. if your aim is even halfway decent this can give you great value in teamfights, however in my opinion it's still the meme pick. the attack speed buff *should* increase your heal speed during Valk/mini-Valk, but there's some debate online about that.\n\n[Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1) gives you basically infinite sustain since again, the buff uptime is infinite during Valk/mini-Valk. this is the best option if *you're* the one getting consistently picked and not the rest of your team.\n\n## \ud83d\udcb0 items\nas Venta explains in [her guide,](https://stadiumbuilds.io/build/e3c4bf87-e8b9-4fe2-bd75-3e3ea6b5d857) at this point in the match, there's not much you can do  for your teammates in terms of raw healing. so, it's best practice to sacrifice a little WP in favor of CDR, movement speed, and survivability. we do this by selling any remaining blues and then picking up a second epic utility item from Round 6: [Ogundimu Reduction Field](item_b12daf48-069b-44c1-88fe-221cbcff664d), [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98), or [Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48)",
